  "title": "Selection and cycle-like composition exclude each other",
  "subject": "Whether any law both selects its spaces (mutual selection) and composes its knots like cycles, and the five weak four-place classes",
  "conclusion": "Each of the five weak four-place classes yields a knot with a forcing place, and two copies sharing that place form a hub, so none composes its knots like cycles. A Boolean law with a knot whose knots compose like cycles is affine, so its count is 2^(n-r) or 0 and it has no mutual selection: selection and cycle-like composition exclude each other.",
